+# DE-N12-SYNTHETIC-01 — proposed N12 synthetic prediction sequencing exception
+
+2026-11-04. **PROPOSED / INACTIVE. This document does not activate N12 implementation, fitting, evaluation, schema/API/UI integration or new prediction execution.**
+
+The current owner directive permits activation only of a valid **preexisting** N12 proposal. Its Phase3 says: “If there is no valid existing proposal, or the proposal grants broader authority than this directive, do not invent an activated replacement or silently bypass the gate.” The pre-change inventory contains14exception records and no N12-specific proposal. This new document makes the missing decision concrete and reviewable; writing it is not owner activation or independent review.
+
+## Original dependencies and purpose
+
+N12 is **Prediction and model evidence**, roadmap requirements **R09/R24/R39/R56**. Its direct prerequisites are **N09 and N11**. Both remain formally In Progress. Their completed synthetic engineering, N11's unpromoted candidates and N07–N10 interfaces do not satisfy full original scientific/source/release prerequisites. Existing N08/N09/N10/N11/N16 exceptions cover their delivered missions only and grant no N12 implementation authority.
+
+If explicitly activated after review, this exception would accommodate sequencing for **one consolidated synthetic/research N12 engineering and acceptance mission**. It would not close any upstream dependency, promote an operational model, approve a diagnosis or waive authentic-source/scientific/hardware/release gates. Formal N12 remains In Progress after implementation unless every original closure requirement is genuinely satisfied.
+
+## Exact proposed scope after activation
+
+- Reuse the current Node/SQLite/application architecture and preserve `linear-trend-v2` and its frozen nominal calibration until an independently inspectable replacement is verified. Document and correct legacy source/window/read-side-effect limitations within the authorized synthetic path; do not rewrite historical evaluation or calibration artifacts.
+- Implement versioned crew-scoped raw-unit and personal-reference-deviation targets, conditional short-horizon projections and deterioration **trajectory evidence**, uncertainty and abstention. The primary six-hour JSON is an example, not a scientifically validated horizon or compulsory numerical threshold. Freeze actual supported targets/horizons and their source-coverage eligibility before scoring.
+- Implement a transparent simple baseline from the permitted linear/robust-trend/quantile or justified regression families. Advanced/temporal methods are conditional on measured benefit and eligible inputs, not mandatory for appearance. No disease forecast, calibrated clinical probability or treatment recommendation. Never reclassify the rejected N11 Isolation Forest as promoted or use its anomaly score as a calibrated forecast.
+- Freeze source identities/hashes/versions, metric units, normalization/reference eligibility, feature definitions, target times, chronological train/calibration/evaluation partitions, thresholds and metrics before candidate execution. Keep labels/future target values out of inference; mechanical fictional separation is not scientific independence. Seen development cases cannot be relabeled as independent validation.
+- Measure MAE, median absolute error, error by supported horizon, empirical interval coverage/calibration, abstention/coverage and relevant trajectory detection errors with honest denominators and undefined results. Compare candidates with the fixed baseline; preserve rejected models and failed qualification. No numerical accuracy band or medical approval is invented. Retain the original <250ms CPU target and measure the actual scope.
+- Preserve observation, recording/knowledge, simulation, issue and horizon/target times. Reject malformed/duplicate/out-of-order/unverified inputs; independently check source age, cadence, gaps, corrections and data eligibility at issue time. Unknown, insufficient, unsupported or stale evidence abstains without implying health. Historical reads may not reveal later observations, corrections, model versions or calibration outcomes.
+- Provide authorized versioned APIs and actual connected application presentation using existing interfaces where compatible: crew, horizon, source/reference/model identity, quality/coverage, projections and uncertainty, reasons for abstention, historical cutoffs, loading/empty/error/denied/cancelled states, provenance and actual durable recovery. Preserve spacecraft/Earth reception semantics and the existing Health Agent boundary. Real installed-browser acceptance is required when the UI is implemented; hardware AC-20 remains separate.
+- Implement bounded explicit prediction/evaluation lifecycle and durable versioned records/artifacts/cards: stable IDs, source/config hashes, idempotency, atomic commitment/readback acknowledgement, correction lineage, cancellation/timeouts, interrupted/failed states and cold recovery without implicit replay. Separate pure inspection from explicit computation/persistence; do not portray the legacy write-capable prediction GET as a qualified operational read interface.
+- Run focused synthetic unit/integration/browser and affected regression QA with positive and negative controls, preservation hashes, bounded temporary stores and measured resources. Fix ordinary implementation errors autonomously within the activated scope. Publish one complete report and STOP after N12.
+
+## Permitted source and consumer boundaries after activation
+
+| Component | Permitted synthetic/research use | Retained restriction |
+|---|---|---|
+| N07 | Pinned authorized local provenance/quality/rights descriptors | Metadata is not forecasting training data; absent Sleep-EDF/PTT/RadLab/named OSD sources, rights and independent grouping/reviews remain open. No new acquisition |
+| N08 | Explicit verified same-crew synthetic source/revision/hash windows or context where relevant | No unverified biomedical feature, clinical waveform calibration, source relabeling or N06 anatomy activation |
+| N09 | Dated fictional references and actual deterministic source observations; separate authored labels and bounded reproducible cases | No clinical realism/generalization claim; original generator and accepted scenario/evaluation histories remain unchanged |
+| N10 | Nonprivate sleep/exercise/context through actual caller authorization and replay contracts | No raw mood, consent, task timing or personal cognitive history through generic prediction/research access. No invented sleep-stage or movement evidence |
+| N11 | Verified saved source/reference/quality/explanation metadata and research-only interface | No promotion/refit of rejected Isolation Forest, no automatic new N11 campaign or transitive model authority |
+| N02 | Unchanged deterministic monitoring and alert evidence for compatibility/noninterference tests | N12 cannot create, modify, suppress, resolve or acknowledge N02 alerts, change thresholds/baselines, or change Earth delivery |
+| N14/N15 | Explicit inactive future evidence-reference interface where useful | No unreviewed support rule, Qwen/LLM inference, prompt promotion or medical-answer integration |
+| N16 | Versioned inactive projection/evidence descriptor for future separately authorized use | No sealed SQLite source, native SQL workers, four-tool replay, operational Health Agent integration or expired startup/resource permissions |
+
+## Required resource and execution preflight
+
+Before any future new N12 candidate execution, record finite fixture sizes and counts, authorized source instances, targets/horizons/windows, train/calibration/evaluation bounds, model complexity, process/heap/deadline/cancellation controls, payload/retention/storage limits and durable output location. State what is enforced versus sampled. Use only fresh memory/OS-temp synthetic application/test databases and a separately designated N12 artifact area. No existing operational database is selected. This proposal supplies **no current worker-startup or resource permission**, and no N11/N16 quota transfers.
+
+Reuse existing installed runtimes and browser tooling. No model/package/browser download, installation, external acquisition/request, mount change, source permission relaxation, private medical record or production deployment. If a required boundary cannot be established, stop that operation without weakening it; complete independent authorized work.
+
+## Review, original gates and exit
+
+Full N09/N11 and their N01/N02/N03/N07/N08/N10/transitive prerequisites remain. N07 authentic source/rights/annotation/independent grouping and scientific review, N08 authentic waveform/release and conditional N06 twin requirements, N03/AC-20 hardware and final release requirements remain unresolved where currently open. N11's rejected-model decision and pending scientific acceptance remain intact. N14/N15 review gates and N16 operational permissions are not changed.
+
+Source presence, a hash, a valid citation, synthetic metric coverage or Codex QA is not an independent scientific/medical approval. Prepare review-ready packets with actual versions and blank reviewer decisions; never fabricate signatures or declare clinical applicability. A future candidate that misses a mandatory performance criterion must stay unqualified; optional advanced-model rejection does not require substituting a clinical claim.
+
+Activation requires an **explicit new owner decision naming this exact existing proposal after review**, including acceptance of its bounded synthetic scope. Any independently required scientific/release approvals remain separate. Fields below are intentionally blank; no new approval is inferred from the current mission.
+
+Owner activation decision:
+
+Decision date and exact reviewed proposal SHA-256:
+
+Reviewed scope/changes:
+
+Independent scientific reviewer, authority, reviewed data/model versions and decision:
+
+No proposal is activated now. If later activated, task authority expires at delivery, owner stop, or an unresolved authorization/source-integrity/security/resource failure. Preserve evidence, record outcomes and STOP; no automatic further N12 run, N13–N16 workstream or operational promotion follows.
